--Description: We need participant‑level DRG2 expression in LGG.  The metric is the average of log10(normalized_count+1)
--             across all samples belonging to the same participant.  In Snowflake, the base‑10 logarithm is obtained
--             with LOG(value, 10).  Therefore: 1) keep rows where Study = 'LGG' and Symbol = 'DRG2'; 
--             2) compute LOG("normalized_count" + 1, 10) for each row; 3) take the AVG of those values per
--             "ParticipantBarcode"; 4) show up to 20 rows for inspection.
